        {
          "source": "https://eco.com/support/en/articles/14798703-optimism-superchain-how-op-stack-works",
          "thread": "Protocol-native L2 land grabs",
          "why": "Uniswap's Unichain, Frax's Fraxtal, CoW Swap on Arbitrum, Polynomial splitting from Synthetix, and Fraxtal announcements all ranked top-10, showing readers treat established DeFi protocols launching their own L2 as a competitive power play worth tracking."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Vitalik's L2 thesis and satire",
          "why": "Four separate Vitalik posts — cross-L2 wallet reads, the global scaling vision, Soneium commentary, and the 'reciprocal tariffs' joke — all cracked the top-20 clicks, signaling readers use his framing as the baseline for judging every L2 announcement."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Bridge and key management exploits",
          "why": "The Profanity-tool DAI deployer compromise (affecting all chains except Optimism and Arbitrum) and Shibarium's permanent $1.7M bridge loss both ranked high, showing readers treat L2 security failures as concrete financial events, not theoretical risk."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "L2 proliferation skepticism",
          "why": "Curve's $1,500/day total L2 returns, the BTC L2 failure thesis, MEV bots dominating L1 gas over L2s, and Vitalik's tariff satire clustered into a readable anti-L2 counter-narrative that drew consistent clicks from readers skeptical of endless rollup sprawl."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://www.zksync.io",
          "thread": "ZK technology race",
          "why": "The $900K Ethereum Foundation ZK grants initiative, Starknet and zkSync user-growth surge, Fhenix's $15M confidentiality L2 raise, and OKX's rumored Polygon zkEVM collaboration formed a sub-story about which ZK approach captures the next cycle."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://polygon.technology/polygon-zkevm",
          "thread": "Corporate and institutional L2 bets",
          "why": "Sony's Soneium paired with a Sony Bank JPY stablecoin, Blast backed by Paradigm and Standard Crypto, and Polygon pitching a $200K/year white-label L2 to ApeCoin pulled readers tracking when large non-native institutions enter the rollup territory race."
        }
      ]
